pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% Regression test: `Clause::add` falls back to a general PB constraint when the degree of
% the sum does not stay 1, and that fallback subtracted the merge cancellation from the
% degree in i64 after checking only the unadjusted sum. Here the degree sum is i64::MIN + 1
% and both variables cancel, so the true degree is i64::MIN - 1; it used to wrap to
% i64::MAX and made the trivially true sum the empty contradiction. The formula is
% satisfiable (x1 true).
f 2 ;
pol 1 2 + ;
output NONE;
conclusion UNSAT : 3 ;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
